NAME
       ftp - file transfer program (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       ftp HOST

DESCRIPTION
       ftp connects to an FTP server (TCP port 21), asks for a user name and a
       password, then shows an ftp> prompt. Many servers allow the user name
       anonymous with any password; they then show only their public folder
       (on vsftpd: /var/ftp, with the pub folder in it).

       In Cyber Range ftp reaches only the range's pretend servers.

COMMANDS
       ls [FOLDER]        list a folder (ls -a also shows hidden files)
       cd FOLDER          change folder
       pwd                show the current folder
       get FILE [LOCAL]   copy a file to the current folder on your box
       binary, ascii      the transfer mode (both work the same here)
       bye                leave (also quit, exit)

EXAMPLES
       ftp 10.10.1.20
       Name: anonymous
       Password: (anything)
       ftp> cd pub
       ftp> get notes.txt
       ftp> bye

NOTES
       FTP sends passwords as plain text. Only test servers you own or have
       written permission to test.

SEE ALSO
       nmap(1), curl(1), scp(1)
